<br><br>
<b>FROM PTRC President Paul Catucci</b>
<br>
<br>
Hello All,
<br><p>
  &nbsp;Our annual Chili contest was held January 27th at 6PM. This year we had 9 entries a little smaller this year but about 40 people enjoyed the best chili in the county. The winner this year was Jim Catucci. Our Judges were Sheriff Rich Giardino, Christian Klueg, and Amanda and Josh Mormile. It was a great night for PTRC and a good time was had by all.
<br>
<br> &nbsp;Many club members that do not receive the newsletter by email did not get the last 2. We had a mix up with our printer and they did not go out. Our apologies, moving forward we hope that is fixed.
<br>
<br> &nbsp;The annual swap shop is on April 24th @ 9:00AM until 3:00PM? It will be same as in the past buy, sell, trade. All local state, federal laws still apply. Last year we had 52 tables and filled the house! We hope to do the same this year. Tables are $10 each for club members or $15.00 for non-members. Call Steven to reserve your table @ (518) 224-3437. The admission to the swap shop is $5.00 each and $2.00 from every entry will go to the Local Boy and Girl Scouts. Kitchen will be open for Breakfast and Lunch, coffee, etc.
<br>
<br>Update on the FMCC Veterans Club to raise money to bring The Vietnam Memorial Traveling Wall to the college. The Pins are out for sale for $5.00 and the Shirts are in house and for sale for $15.00. All money raised will go for the cause or LOCAL VETERANS in need. We already received 40 shirt sponsors. This is a record. The cost of this effort is over $10,000. PTRC will get their goal most of the way there with some great people that have already donated. If you would like to help call us. We are proud of all our Veterans, many of our members were in Vietnam.
<br>
<br> &nbsp;The next Leather Stocking honor Flight is May 7th. If you never went to Albany International Airport for this ceremony it is well worth the time. It last less than an hour.  PTRC will send the check for the money we raised throughout the year. We are very close to the $1500.00 mark! Thanks to in part, the efforts of Nick Valachovic. If you know anyone that was in WWII or Korea and would like to travel to Washington to see their Memorial free of charge contact Nick for the form.
<br>
<br> &nbsp;Dues update, about 175 folks are late as of NOW. A late fee of $10 will be added at this time. Please pay ASAP, we are over 1000 members with a waiting list. You can make Steven's life easy stop at the club any Monday night or Wednesday to pay dues.
<br>
<br> &nbsp;When is the last time you attended a PTRC meeting? Our members are what make us great. You have a lot to offer and we need your help. This club belongs to all our members! Next meetings are February 10th &amp; March 9th @ 7:00PM. Annual Spaghetti Supper February 17 @6PM pre-sale only. Tickets are at the bar.   Next regular supper March 16th @ 6:30PM.
<br>
<br> &nbsp;Pistol License Classes are held the first Wednesday of the month. Club members are $10.00 and non-members are $15.00 for the 3 hour class with live fire. So far this year we have had 48 for January, 48 for February and it looks like March will fill soon. The max is 48 we will take.
<br>
<br> &nbsp;The Annual Raffle Tickets are out! This is the only fund raiser we do for ourselves. Things are a little different this year. We offer the cash on odd days ($300) and on even cash ($300) or a gift card from Runnings for $450. Highest seller wins $300.00, sell 40 tickets free dues for 2017. Get a pack of 5, 10, up to 40 at a time. See Paul Christman or myself.
 <br>
 <br> &nbsp;Visit us on Facebook, check out our ever changing website www.pinetreerifleclub.org.
 <br>
 <br><b>My contacts are <a href="mailto:paul.catucci@gmail.com">Email paul.catucci@gmail.com</a> or phone (518)649-7617</b>
</p>
